# Admin Navigation Button Group Layout

- **Use the shared navigation**
  - Use [`AdminNavigation.tsx`](mdc:src/components/AdminNavigation.tsx) for reusable admin navigation groups.
  - Treat `/admin/manage-events` as the reference for the compact button-group width.

- **Keep the group constrained**
  - The navigation container must use `w-full max-w-5xl mx-auto`.
  - Preserve an explicit `maxWidth: '64rem'` because `.admin-navigation-container` in [`globals.css`](mdc:src/app/globals.css) sets `max-width: 100%`.
  - Full-width page wrappers are allowed, but the navigation group itself must not stretch across the viewport.

```tsx
// ✅ DO
<div
  className="w-full max-w-5xl mx-auto admin-navigation-container"
  style={{ width: '100%', maxWidth: '64rem' }}
>
  {/* navigation grid */}
</div>
```

- **Prevent hydration expansion**
  - Any mount effect that writes container dimensions must preserve `maxWidth = '64rem'`.
  - Never reset the shared navigation container to `maxWidth = '100%'` after hydration.

```tsx
// ❌ DON'T
containerRef.current.style.maxWidth = '100%';

// ✅ DO
containerRef.current.style.maxWidth = '64rem';
```

- **Maintain vertical alignment**
  - On `/admin/manage-events`, keep the Back to Admin button aligned with the navigation cards using responsive left spacing matching the navigation panel padding.
  - On `/admin/events/registrations`, place the Back to Admin button and page title above the shared navigation inside the same `max-w-5xl` alignment frame.
  - Add `pt-4 sm:pt-6` to the registrations header/navigation wrapper so the fixed site header does not clip the top of the Back button or title.
  - On `/admin`, retain top padding on the title in both loading and authenticated render branches so the fixed header does not clip it.

```tsx
// ✅ DO — protect the registrations header from the fixed site header
<div className="w-full pt-4 sm:pt-6 px-2 sm:px-3 md:px-4 lg:px-6 xl:px-8">
  <div className="max-w-5xl mx-auto px-2.5 sm:px-3 md:px-4 lg:px-6 xl:px-8">
    {/* Back button and title */}
  </div>
  <AdminNavigation currentPage="event-registrations" />
</div>
```

- **Verify**
  - Check width immediately after initial render and again after hydration completes.
  - Confirm `/admin/manage-events` and `/admin/events/registrations` display the same navigation-group width.
  - Confirm the registrations Back button and title remain fully visible below the fixed site header at mobile and desktop widths.
